 "text": "9/29/26, 9:47 AM\n\n\u2014 Recommendation\nIf you want to distinguish between Winter weekdays and Winter weekends when you execute the components, but you want\n\nSummer weekdays and Summer weekends to be treated equally, define the parameter allocations of the component codes\nWinter Weekdays, Winter Weekends, and Default. The default parameter alllocations are used for Summer weekdays and\n\nSummer Weekends.\n\nExample: RTP Interface with Formula COPYO1\n\nComponent                              Description                              Priority                                    Activation Type\n\nON/OFF                                     Calculation of On-Peak/Off-           1                                               Use and activate generally\nPeak Consumption\n\nMAX                                         Determine Max. Demand              2                                              Use and activate generally\n\n(E)RTP Interface RTP1\n\nEARTP Component ON/OFF\n\n\u00b0  Gy RTP Component Code On-Peak Consumption\n\u00b0  Ld | Input Parameter 1 Consumption Profile - Quantity\n\u00b0   [ee Output Parameter 1 Copy of Consumption Profile\n\u00b0  Lea | Output Parameter 2 Copy as Demand Profile\n\n\u00a2 (@@RTP Component Code Off-Peak Consumption\n)  Ld | Input Parameter 1 Consumption Profile - Quantity\n\u00b0   ee Output Parameter 1 Copy of Consumption Profile\n\n\u00b0  Lea | Output Parameter 2 Copy as Demand Profile\n\ne GBy@RTP Component Code Default\n\n\u00b0  Ld | Input Parameter 1 Consumption Profile - Quantity\n\u00b0  Lea | Output Parameter 1 Copy as Demand Profile\n\n\u00b0  Lea | Output Parameter 2 Copy as Demand Profile\n\nEARTP Component MAX\ne GByG@RTP Component Code Default\n\u00b0  Le Input Parameter 1 Consumption Profile - Quantity\n\u00b0   Lea | Output Parameter 1 Copy of Consumption Profile\n\n\u00b0  ee Output Parameter 2 Copy as Demand Profile\n",
